title: McCabe Complexity Metric (pmccabe / GNU complexity tool)
authors: Multiple (pmccabe by Paul Oman; GNU complexity by Bruce Korb)
year: 1994
venue: unix/linux tools; pmccabe manpage, GNU complexity
quality: CODE
url: https://manpages.ubuntu.com/manpages/focal/man1/pmccabe.1.html
keywords: pmccabe, GNU complexity, McCabe cyclomatic complexity, C, C++, non-commented lines
cites: McCabe 1976
cited_by:
content:
  pmccabe: Computes McCabe cyclomatic complexity for C/C++ programs.
    Output: per-function modified cyclomatic complexity (MCC) and NCSL.
    Modified complexity (mccabe's "strict" mode): counts each case in switch.
    Also provides non-commented source lines (NCSL).
    Decision nodes counted: if, while, for, do, case, ?, ||, &&
  
  GNU complexity (https://www.gnu.org/software/complexity/):
    Measures complexity of C source code.
    Based on McCabe's original formula.
    Default maximum: 10 (triggers warning).
    Features: per-function complexity, histogram output.
  
  THRESHOLD: Both default to 10 as the warning threshold.
<<<END>>>

SOURCE
id: 29
ts: 2026-05-29T00:25:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Metric Summary Table: Computation from CFG/Dominators/Def-Use for pflow
authors: (synthesized record for pflow reference)
year: 2026
venue: pflow project notes
quality: DOCS
url:
keywords: CFG, dominators, post-dominators, def-use, PDG, metric computation, pflow
cites: all above sources
cited_by:
content:
  METRIC -> WHAT IT NEEDS -> HOW TO COMPUTE -> SIMPLIFICATION SIGNAL
  
  V(G) [Cyclomatic Complexity]:
    Needs: CFG
    Compute: E - N + 2  (edges - nodes + 2) for single function
    Signal: V(G) > 10 = too many independent paths; decompose function
  
  ev(G) [Essential Complexity]:
    Needs: CFG + T1-T2 reduction (or interval analysis)
    Compute: Iteratively remove single-entry/single-exit subgraphs (structured primes)
             until no more removable. V(G) of remaining graph = ev(G).
    Signal: ev(G) > 1 = unstructured jumps; ev(G) - 1 = number of
            non-structurable constructs. pflow target: reduce ev(G) to 1.
  
  Cognitive Complexity:
    Needs: CFG (structured with nesting depth tracking) + lexical structure
    Compute: DFS on AST/CFG; at each control structure:
             increment += 1 + nesting_depth (structural);
             or += 1 (hybrid/fundamental);
             boolean sequences += 1 per sequence type.
    Signal: > 15 = hard to understand; deeply nested code = nesting penalty.
  
  NPATH:
    Needs: CFG (hierarchical, no loops collapsed)
    Compute: Recursive formula per statement type (multiplicative for sequences,
             additive for branches). See record id:4 for full formula table.
    Signal: > 200 = needs decomposition; exponential sensitivity to nesting.
  
  Knots:
    Needs: Linearized program text + control-flow arcs
    Compute: Count crossing pairs of arcs in linear order.
             (i->j) and (k->l) cross if i<k<j<l or k<i<l<j.
    Signal: > 0 = unstructured; knots = pairs of crossing jumps.
  
  Nesting Depth (max):
    Needs: CFG or AST
    Compute: Max depth of nesting counter during traversal.
    Signal: > 3-4 = deeply nested; each level removed improves cognitive complexity.
  
  DepDegree:
    Needs: CFG + reaching definitions (def-use graph)
    Compute: dd(G) = |E| in use-def graph S_G.
             Per statement: count how many definitions reach each use.
             dd_G(s) = sum_x |rd(s,x)| for all vars x used in s.
    Signal: High-dd statements = many dependencies; scope reduction helps.
  
  Variable Span / Live Range:
    Needs: CFG + def-use chains
    Compute: For each var x: distance (statements) from each def to last use.
             Average span = avg statements between successive uses.
             Live range overlap = simultaneously live variables at each point.
    Signal: Long spans = move definitions closer to uses; reduce scope.
  
  Halstead Volume:
    Needs: Token stream (lexer)
    Compute: V = N * log2(n) where N = total tokens, n = distinct tokens.
    Signal: V > 1000 per function (guideline); reduce by decomposition.
  
  Halstead Difficulty:
    Needs: Token stream
    Compute: D = (n1/2) * (N2/n2) where n1=distinct ops, N2=total operands, n2=distinct operands.
    Signal: High D = error-prone; reduce by reducing operand reuse rate.
  
  Slice Cohesion:
    Needs: CFG + def-use + post-dominators (for slicing)
    Compute: Backward slice for each output variable; measure intersection of slices.
    Signal: Low intersection = independent slices = natural split points = Extract Method.
  
  Control Dependence Fan-out:
    Needs: PDG (post-dominator frontier computation)
    Compute: For each predicate p: count statements control-dependent on p.
    Signal: Large fan-out = predicate controls too many things; refactor the branch condition.
  
  DATA FLOW COMPLEXITY (Oviedo):
    Needs: CFG + reaching definitions
    Compute: DF(P) = |{(d,u) : d defines x, u uses x, d reaches u}| over all vars.
    Signal: High DF = many def-use pairs to track; reduce variable scope or split function.
<<<END>>>


